# fixedbugs, defect 591, lane b20-pragma, 2026-10-11, found by lane b19-pack
# beside defect 582: the header renames the bound `labs` by `#pragma
# redefine_extname`, and the linker cannot find the name it gives. On this
# Mac `redefine_extname labs llabs` failed so, the label having none of
# Mach-O's underscore, and in the Linux arm64 image it links; this twin names
# a symbol no platform has. Until then the link said *internal error* at exit
# 2, the missing name being no group's; it is now read back to the binding
# through clang's dump of the header list (`cli/renamed.hero`). Defect 640,
# lane b21-win, 2026-10-11: it bound `labs` from `<stdlib.h>`, whose `long`
# is 32 bits on Windows, so `labs(x: i64)` was refused there before the link;
# the header declares the function it renames, at `long long`.

extern "fixedbugs-591-a-bound-function-a-header-renames-by-redefine-extname-is-told.h"
    function fixedbugs_591_renamed(x: i64) -> i64  #~ ffi_missing_link

function main()
    print(fixedbugs_591_renamed(x: -42))
